# The BusyBox shell's start-up file in term51 (its ENV). The prompt is ash's
# own (\w \$), with the shell's directory reported to the terminal before it
# in the standard way (OSC 7, a file URL), from which the tab is named while
# the shell waits at its prompt. \[ and \] keep the report out of the
# prompt's width; $PWD is read at each prompt.
PS1='\[\e]7;file://${PWD}\a\]\w \$ '
